 {
  "id": "e:lege skjul|phrase#1",
  "kind": "example",
  "unit": "entry:lege skjul|phrase",
  "passed": false,
  "stage": "review",
  "problems": [
   "translations: English 'hide and seek' should be hyphenated as 'hide-and-seek' to match the Danish 'skjul' (a single game). The provided translation 'hide and seek' is a common variant, but the standard is 'hide-and-seek'. However, this is a minor spelling preference, not a real defect. The real defect is that the Russian translation 'Дети каждый день после обеда играют в прятки в саду' adds 'после обеда' (after lunch) which is not in the Danish 'hver eftermiddag' (every afternoon). The Danish says 'hver eftermiddag' (every afternoon), not 'после обеда'. Similarly, Ukrainian 'щодня після обіду' adds 'після обіду' (after lunch). The translations are not faithful; they add information not present in the original.",
   "adjudicator: The Russian and Ukrainian translations incorrectly add 'после обеда'/'після обіду' (after lunch), which is not present in the Danish 'hver eftermiddag' (every afternoon)."
  ]
 },
